          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"category\":\"persistent LVDS channel dropout\",\"cause\":\"Unknown. The leading hypothesis is loss of the LVDS signal on pin 16, affecting detector channels 32/33, potentially from a disconnected or degraded pin, jumper, cable, or source output. An intentional configuration or masking condition is an alternative.\",\"action\":\"First verify whether pin 16 and channels 32/33 are intentionally disabled or masked. If not, stop the run and inspect/reseat the pin-16 LVDS connection, jumper wires, and associated digitizer/trigger-board cables. Then start a new diagnostic run and confirm that pin-16 counts, channels 32/33 data presence, and board matching return to expected behavior. If reseating does not restore the signal, test the source output and swap with a known-good cable/input to localize the fault.\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"supporting_historical_runs\":[1747,2068,2071,2126],\"reasoning_summary\":\"OBSERVED: LVDS pin 16 is persistently zero/abnormally low and maps exactly to channels 32/33, which are repeatedly reported missing and show waveform-feature anomalies. Other signal pins have similar nonzero medians, while the total trigger rate is stable. Channels 32/33 are also masked, but whether that is intentional or a response to the fault is unknown. INFERRED: This strongly localizes the problem to one LVDS path rather than a detector-wide rate or DAQ failure. A physical connection failure resembles runs 2068, 2071, 2126, and the cable component of 1747, but no historical case is an exact match because those cases involved noise, rate, or board-matching effects rather than a documented persistent zero pin. CONTRADICTING/ALTERNATIVE: Static masking could explain an intentional absence, and board-matching telemetry is unavailable. DISCRIMINATING CHECKS: verify intended mask state, inspect raw pin-16 behavior across the subrun-201 transition, check board matching, and perform cable/input swaps.\"}"
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
